Write a function gcd_times_pc that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers a and b and returns gcd(a, b) times the number of one bits of b. Write and use a helper function gcd(a, b) that returns the greatest common divisor by repeated remainders (gcd(a, 0) = a, gcd(0, 0) = 0). Write and use a helper function popcnt(x) that returns how many of the 32 bits of x are 1. Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
